    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42e0c674_7630b9a8",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3030,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-05T15:49:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Initially this block was added to mimic what happens in SRC_ACCESSORY state\n\t\t\t/* If accessory becomes detached */\n\t\t\tif ((pd[port].cc_state \u003d\u003d PD_CC_AUDIO_ACC \u0026\u0026\n\t\t\t     (cc1 !\u003d TYPEC_CC_VOLT_RA ||\n\t\t\t      cc2 !\u003d TYPEC_CC_VOLT_RA)) ||\n\t\t\t    (pd[port].cc_state \u003d\u003d PD_CC_DEBUG_ACC \u0026\u0026\n\t\t\t     (cc1 !\u003d TYPEC_CC_VOLT_RD ||\n\t\t\t      cc2 !\u003d TYPEC_CC_VOLT_RD))) {\n\t\t\t\tset_state(port, PD_STATE_SRC_DISCONNECTED);\n#if defined(CONFIG_CASE_CLOSED_DEBUG) || defined(CONFIG_USB_PD_DTS)\n\t\t\t\tccd_set_mode(CCD_MODE_DISABLED);\n#endif\n\t\t\t\ttimeout \u003d 10*MSEC;\n\t\t\t}\n\nIf only checking for the detach on CC1 is sufficient, then this can be removed. I moved the call to \u0027ccd_set_mode\u0027 to the if (cc1 \u003d\u003d TYPEC_CC_VOLT_OPEN) { }  section as suggested.",
      "parentUuid": "dc797b93_1aaeb5ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3020,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3030,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "34d23bc05e9aae076ba24ab202d3da918109b05e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d260ce4_1cd8ae4c",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3030,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-05T17:26:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this check is removed, then it becomes more difficult for servo_v4 to force a detach event. For example, when connected to a DUT, when all the Rp/Rd gpio controls are set to input, CC1/CC2 read at ~50mV which gets converted to Ra for CC1/CC2 state. This means that changing dts mode from on to off and vice versa, servo_v4 DUT port will remain in the SRC_READY state. However, by explicitly checking for CC1/CC2 \u003d\u003d Rd, then it will go to SRC_DISCONNECTED. Otherwise there needs to be an actual cable detach.",
      "parentUuid": "42e0c674_7630b9a8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3020,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3030,
        "endChar": 6
      },
